## Running the Project

Install the required dependencies:

```bash
pip install pandas scikit-learn
```

Run the machine learning implementation:

```bash
python3 main.py
```

The program processes the dataset, trains three classification models, and displays their evaluation results.

## Key Findings

- Starbucks recorded the highest average sound level at 58.27 dBA.
- The Library recorded the lowest average sound level at 37.49 dBA.
- Quiet was the most common classification category.
- Decision Tree achieved the highest overall accuracy at 75.46%.
- Random Forest and Logistic Regression performed better at identifying Loud measurements.
- Class imbalance and closely spaced observations may affect model generalization.

## Conclusion

This project demonstrates the application of supervised machine learning to environmental sound classification.

Among the three algorithms, **Decision Tree achieved the best overall performance**, while Random Forest and Logistic Regression showed stronger detection of Loud noise.

The results demonstrate the importance of comparing multiple evaluation metrics when selecting a machine learning model.

